{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482055-alternative-v-tm-creating-new-clans","id":1482055,"title":"Alternative V:tM - Creating New Clans","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-05-26T21:13:55-07:00","id":1482055,"title":"Alternative V:tM - Creating New Clans","content":"Years and years ago, I created a thread where, as a game of sorts, people collaborated to create an alternative V:tM setting. By creating new Clans. I thought it\u2019s been enough years, it might be fun to play that game again.<br /> <br /> Sometimes there are threads or discussions about alternate versions of various OWoD games, like randomly assigning Clans to the Camarilla and Sabbat or eliminating all mages. Well, this will be a similar but perhaps more collaborative thread. Creating our own Clans from scratch and filling up the Camarilla and Sabbat with them. So, there will be 13 Clans, including 7 in the Camarilla and 2 for the Sabbat, plus 4 independents. The Camarilla and Sabbat will be at least similar to the canon organizations in that the Camarilla will represent the rule by elders and will be more conservative and following the Masquerade, while the Sabbat will have been born of the Anarch Revolts, will be more radical, and ostensibly values freedom from the elders. Of course, with different Clans, these organizations will be quite different from canon and important ways.<br /> <br /> We can start by each person essentially taking a turn by creating a Clan with its name, Disciplines, weakness, the sect it belongs to, and adding some brief description. Subsequent turns will add additional Clans, creating them as to fit into the Camarilla or Sabbat along with those Clans added previously. As more turns are taken (assuming he thread takes off) the differences between this setting and canon V:tM will become more fleshed out. Bloodlines can be added as well, along with Clan variants and schisms. Just try not to step on anybody else's toes if you add something to what they've created before you. If the thread lasts long enough to create all 13 Clans, we can flesh out other aspects of this Alt V:tM, like how the Anarch Revolts happened, differences in cosmology, and so on.<br /> <br /> I'll start with an example Clan.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:28px\">Pontiki</span><br /> The Pontiki have always been a Clan that have lived amongst the lower levels of society. Beggars, refugees, oppressed minorities, the homeless. The Pontiki embraced from among these people and considered them their flock, feeding from them but also protecting them from the worst excesses of the more powerful members of society. As the Pontiki empathized with the plight of struggling mortals, they soon too began to side with the plight of struggling vampires and were among those who lead the Anarch revolts and helped to create the Sabbat. Though they often eschew material wealth, they are masterful spies, information brokers, and assassins - often trading in favors rather than money.<br /> <br /> <b>Nickname</b>: Rats<br /> <br /> <b>Sect</b>: the Pontiki are a Sabbat Clan, one of the founders of the Sabbat in fact and are still heavily influential in the Sect. There are also numerous Pontiki who are independent since they object to the Sabbat\u2019s hierarchy or their treatment of mortals. Very few Pontiki are in the Camarilla, though some side with the Anarchs in their attempts to undermine Camarilla rule.<br /> <br /> <b>Appearance</b>: Pontiki come from all ethnic and cultural backgrounds, they are quite diverse in that regard, though groups that are poorer, oppressed, or otherwise disadvantaged are over represented among the Pontiki. Since they have poor backgrounds, they tend to dress on fashions popular within those subcultures. Even among Pontiki who have some measure of wealth and power, they will give the appearance of poverty or at least styles that are popular among poorer or outcast people.<br /> <br /> <b>Haven</b><br /> Many Pontiki live in abandoned buildings, in makeshift shelters, or in vehicles like vans or trucks. It isn\u2019t uncommon for a number of Pontiki to have their haven within a large dilapidated factory or warehouse. Sometimes they may live among homeless or in homes owned by gangs or outlaws.<br /> <br /> <b>Background</b><br /> Pontiki childer are nearly always selected from the poorest members of society. In modern America, this could mean the homeless, immigrants, convicts and criminals, the insane, crippled people, addicts, or runaways. In various times and places they have drawn from slaves, religious or ethnic minorities, or itinerate laborers. Over the years, the Clan has a culture of eschewing material wealth even when the means exist for gaining it.<br /> <br /> <b>Clan Disciplines</b>: Animalism, Celerity, Obfuscate<br /> <br /> <b>Weakness</b>: the blood of the Pontiki has never been able to create a blood bond. Perhaps this weakness, which dates back to time immemorial, was the reason that the Pontiki struggled to gain temporal power and so found solace among the dregs of society.<br /> <br /> <b>Organization</b>: the Pontiki are not highly organized, in fact they often reject the notion of hierarchies, though they are a tightly knit Clan and informally help each other in times of need and show respect to their elders and other Pontiki of noteworthy skill or reputation. In practice they must sometimes obey the will of superiors both within and outside of the Clan, though they often chafe against these situations.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Current Progress:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Camarilla:</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Cicatrix: Auspex, Dominate, Obfuscate</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Netjeru: Dominate, Fortitude, Necromancy</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Dracul: Daimoinon, Protean, Sorcery</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Bagava: Animalism, Potence, Presence</span><br /> Sukkal: Animalism, Auspex, Celerity<br /> Vegulans: None<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Sabbat</b>:</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Pontiki: Animalism, Celerity, Obfuscate</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Polyergus: Auspex, Presence, Vicissitude </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Independant</b>:</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Cecaelia: Fortitude, Presence, Protean</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Hags: Animalism, Obfuscate, Sorcery</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Bloodlines</b>:</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Mara-Ma: Fortitude, Potence, Vicissitude</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Savages: Fortitude, Potence, Protean<br /> Strix: Celerity, Fortitude, Potence<br /> Children of Veles: Carnophagia, Obfuscate, Potence</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1129,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","user":"Sergeant Brother","date":". 09-12-2022, 11:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-26T22:03:58-07:00","id":1482057,"title":"","content":"The Pontiki Clan sounds pretty cool, their weakness and Discipline spread are neat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27083-truemrmultiverse","name":"TrueMrMultiverse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27083_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-26T22:06:19-07:00","id":1482059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TrueMrMultiverse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482055-alternative-v-tm-creating-new-clans?p=1482057#post1482057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Pontiki Clan sounds pretty cool, their weakness and Discipline spread are neat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you \ud83d\ude01","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-26T22:18:16-07:00","id":1482060,"title":"","content":"The Hags<br /> A matriarchal clan that lives mainly in the sewers in modern times, and lived in dank, hidden places like the swamps in ancient times. These hideous creatures hoard arcane dark magical secrets.<br /> <br /> Clan Disciplines: Animalism, Thaumaturgy, Obfuscate<br /> <br /> Weakness: all Hags are hideous, looking like decrepit caricatures of witches.<br /> <br /> Organization: Hags organize into covens centered around the eldest female in the territory.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-26T22:24:05-07:00","id":1482061,"title":"","content":"The Savages<br /> A feral clan known for tearing their prey to pieces.<br /> <br /> Clan Disciplines: Potence, Fortitude, Protean<br /> <br /> Weakness: a Savage's bite embraces anyone they kill. Consequently, they must rip apart anyone they fatally drain as birth control.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-27T07:19:44-07:00","id":1482071,"title":"","content":"Well, I can give it a shot.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Cicatrices</u><br /> singular: Cicatrix</b><br /> <br /> (I'm no good at names, but whatever, White Wolf's choices seemed kin of weird to me half the time. So I named a bunch of vampires &quot;scar tissue&quot;)<br /> <br /> <b>Curse:</b> Flesh of the Corpse. As per the flaw, these vampires cannot heal properly. The health track can be recovered, but wounds leave ugly necrotic-looking gashes and holes, and limbs do not regenerate. Clan horror stories tell of the fools who've been reduced to nothing but a head attached to a dead heart, who will remain so for the rest of eternity. <br /> When they use the blush of life, any wounds they have start bleeding, costing an extra blood point on top of that spent to activate the blush.<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> Dominate, Fortitude, Auspex. <br /> When the rest of your untrustworthy bloodthirsty kind have a significant advantage, controling others is vital. Likewise being able to avoid getting hurt in the first place is ideal, and monitoring thoughts and emotions certainly helps with that. Astral projection and possession are also invaluable in never having to leave a well fortified haven. It's also not uncommon to find Celerity and Obfuscate out-of-clan amongst these vampires; can't hurt you if they can't catch or find you either! (and auspex, which I somehow forgot existed)<br /> <br /> <b>Sect:</b> Camarilla. Being so... delicate, these kindred are more aware than any other the value of a peaceful, stable and well controlled status-quo. They tend to lend their abilities to making sure the Ivory Tower lives up to those values. They keep a keen eye on events and individuals, making sure nobody rocks the boat. <i>Or else.</i><br /> <br /> Many of these vampires keep a staff of carefully conditioned spies and bodyguards to protect themselves. <br /> <br /> Childer are typically picked from those who serve the needs of the sire, clan and sect. People who show themselves capable in maintaining the environment the clan needs. Often they come from the sire's ghoul retinue, going through a period of assessment and grooming - followed by yet another one after the embrace.<br /> <br /> A lot of them develop intense paranoia and control problems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 05-29-2022, 09:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-27T10:29:24-07:00","id":1482079,"title":"","content":"CECAELIA<br /> First spotted in the ancient Mediterranean but now thought to have inspired tales of sea monsters around the world, this secretive breed of Kindred enchants, devastates, and disappears beneath the depths from which they came.<br /> <br /> Nickname: Sirens<br /> <br /> Sect: Independent. The Cecaelia are a force to be reckoned with in many coastal Camarilla or Sabbat domains, extorting tribute and concessions from Kindred whose fortunes depend on maritime trade and tourism.<br /> <br /> Appearance: Many Cecaelia either shun clothing entirely when not on land, or wear the clothes they were embraced in - water sport gear, diving apparel, and naval uniforms are not uncommon.<br /> Some who wish to play up the legendary enchanter of the sea may keep a collection of waterlogged apparel in their havens, but shiny jewelry, whose sparkling could be mistaken for prey fish, is nearly never worn unless the Cecaelia is in the mood to hunt a shark.<br /> <br /> Haven: The ability to sink safely into the sea floor is a part of every Cecaelia's birthright, but many find or submerge some sort of large container until they learn the power - or if they have treasures they wish to store.<br /> <br /> Background: Humans have worked or played on the water for ages; modern archaeology has even uncovered evidence that Neanderthal Man built and used working sailboats and explored. A Cecaelia could come from nearly any conceivable walk of life, with selection for the Embrace depending entirely on the whims of the individual sire. Infatuation and longing are often the motivation, and the Sirens have a reputation for beauty when they put on their game faces. Social Attributes and Skills are usually predominant, with Physical Attributes and Talents a close second.<br /> <br /> Clan Disciplines: Fortitude, Presence, Protean (Mariner variant)<br /> <br /> Weakness: An eternity spent submerged and subsisting on the blood of fishes and sharks takes its toll. Neonates merely look freshly drowned, but features of fish and other horrors intermingle with the once-human to disturbing effect as the years wear on. A Cecaelia's Appearance score only counts when the Siren is actively spending blood to appear human (V20, p. 269) for a scene. In all other scenarios, the Siren's Appearance score is effectively zero and they cannot pass for a normal human.<br /> <br /> Note that one of the Discipline powers for which the clan is best known (Entrancement, V20 p. 195) uses Appearance + Empathy for a dice pool, and this is when the ability of the blood to pass for human sees the most use among the Cecaelia.<br /> <br /> Organization: A great many Cecaelia are Autarkis, dwelling alone in lakes and rivers where the feeding isn't abundant enough to sustain more. Whole broods can be encountered in bays and on the shoreline near cities, where the flow of traffic is rich.<br /> <br /> The extent to which the clan has any organization beyond that is unknown, but the best way to hide a secret is to put it under the ocean...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","user":"Reasor","date":". 05-27-2022, 01:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-27T10:50:13-07:00","id":1482081,"title":"","content":"I had a clan nicknamed &quot;Los Perdidos&quot; who actually managed to kill their antidiluvian becoming &quot;da true anarchs&quot;. Similar to the Pontiki they can neither create blood bonds. They are the chaos factor into the masquerade but the lack of organization from the clan makes them be labeled as caitiff many times specially by the brujah who are jealous from their feat.<ul><li>Nightmare (From requiem, fear and subconscius manipulation)</li> <li>Venandi (Miscellaneus powers who include flight)</li> <li>Vigor/Potence</li> </ul><br /> <b>Bane </b><ul><li>Los perdidos cannot create ghouls or blood bond people</li> <li>Los perdidos have a -1 penalty to degeneration roll</li> </ul><br /> <br /> Note: They also have a merit bloodline that gives them access to infernalism on creation if they start with humanity 5 as there are some infernalist cults among them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-27T11:17:22-07:00","id":1482085,"title":"","content":"I was flirting with homebrewing a clans based on Tah-tah-kle\u2019-ah and skadegamutc native american myths as a pre Colombian clans but considering the blowback on wendigo and Im British anyway i decided against it.<br /> I did however introduce the daeva and mekhet as ashirra aligned clans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-27T11:26:54-07:00","id":1482086,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:36px\">Yara-Ma</span><br /> The Yara-Ma of Australian wilds are little known, and less cared for. Kindred view them as a dangerous threat for their ability to walk around in the sun without fear. Despite this, members of the bloodline rarely take part in vampiric politics, and often prefer to sleep in fig trees most days, where they wait for mortals to rest under before they attack. Their ability to walk in the sun makes many believe that they are not in fact kindred at all.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Nickname:</b> Drop Bears</span><br /> <br /> <b>Sect:</b><span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> The Drop Bears rarely participate in modern politics and will rarely join the Sabbat or Camarilla. However, both sects will often hire the Yara-Ma as day-time assassins.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Appearance:</b><span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> Yara-Ma often twist their features and traits to look more koala like to become less noticeable in the trees. However, just as many in the clan will take their time to look especially monstrous if given the chance.<br /> <br /> <b>Haven:</b> The Drops Bears often hunt in the wilds and will most often make their home within trees and caves. The bloodline often prefers to sleep in fig trees, a practice taught from sire to childer.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Background:</b> Yara-Ma only embrace individuals who show a resilience and ability to survive harsh environments. People who resist their feeding are often embraced after a long observational period.<br /> <br /> <b>Clan Disciplines: </b>Fortitude, Potence, Vicissitude<br /> <br /> <b>Weakness: </b>The Yara-Ma have nothing to fear from the sun, and do not need to sleep during the day. However, they instead feel the urge to sleep at night and often will not wake without great difficulty. The Drop Bear\u2019s Humanity/Path rating is considered 2 dots lower for waking and remaining active at night. This weakness is the primary reason the drop bears do not take part in the undead's politics.<br /> <br /> <b>Organization:</b> Drop Bears are solitary by nature and will only mentor their childer for a month at most.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-27T11:38:28-07:00","id":1482087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482055-alternative-v-tm-creating-new-clans?p=1482085#post1482085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did however introduce the daeva and mekhet as ashirra aligned clans.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds like one of the best places to put them, but did they not overlap with the original clans?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-27T12:25:04-07:00","id":1482092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482055-alternative-v-tm-creating-new-clans?p=1482087#post1482087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds like one of the best places to put them, but did they not overlap with the original clans?</div> </div> </div> </div>I just changed daevas celerity to auspex and emphasised geographic origin, their was something of a plot point that deavas had strong links with classical Persian culture (including an underlying issue the clan is historically supportive of Shia and zorostrinianism) mekhet fitted in pretty well, there was a split between coptic Christian, Muslim with some ancient pagans in the eldars. I decided they explicitly rejected cultural links with setites or osiris considering mekhet a standard 3rd gen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 05-27-2022, 03:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-27T13:16:35-07:00","id":1482100,"title":"","content":"Good responses y\u2019all. Let me see if I can order things a little to create a coherent alternative setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482055-alternative-v-tm-creating-new-clans?p=1482060#post1482060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Hags<br /> A matriarchal clan that lives mainly in the sewers in modern times, and lived in dank, hidden places like the swamps in ancient times. These hideous creatures hoard arcane dark magical secrets.<br /> <br /> Clan Disciplines: Animalism, Thaumaturgy, Obfuscate<br /> <br /> Weakness: all Hags are hideous, looking like decrepit caricatures of witches.<br /> <br /> Organization: Hags organize into covens centered around the eldest female in the territory.</div> </div> </div> </div>These are cool, but they could use a few more details. What Sect are they in? What do they do?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482055-alternative-v-tm-creating-new-clans?p=1482061#post1482061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Savages<br /> A feral clan known for tearing their prey to pieces.<br /> <br /> Clan Disciplines: Potence, Fortitude, Protean<br /> <br /> Weakness: a Savage's bite embraces anyone they kill. Consequently, they must rip apart anyone they fatally drain as birth control.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that these will need to be a bloodline. They are just too dangerous to the Masquerade and have too few social abilities to be a major part of the vampire world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482055-alternative-v-tm-creating-new-clans?p=1482071#post1482071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I can give it a shot.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Cicatrices</u><br /> singular: Cicatrix</b><br /> <br /> (I'm no good at names, but whatever, White Wolf's choices seemed kin of weird to me half the time. So I named a bunch of vampires &quot;scar tissue&quot;)<br /> <br /> <b>Curse:</b> Flesh of the Corpse. As per the flaw, these vampires cannot heal properly. The health track can be recovered, but wounds leave ugly necrotic-looking gashes and holes, and limbs do not regenerate. Clan horror stories tell of the fools who've been reduced to nothing but a head attached to a dead heart, who will remain so for the rest of eternity.<br /> When they use the blush of life, any wounds they have start bleeding, costing an extra blood point on top of that spent to activate the blush.<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> Dominate, Fortitude, Obfuscate.<br /> When the rest of your untrustworthy bloodthirsty kind have a significant advantage, controling others is vital. Likewise being able to avoid getting hurt in the first place is ideal, and they can't hurt you if they can't find you. It's also not uncommon to find Celerity out-of-clan amongst these vampires; can't kill you if they can't catch you either! (and auspex, which I somehow forgot existed)<br /> <br /> <b>Sect:</b> Camarilla. Being so... delicate, these kindred are more aware than any other the value of a peaceful, stable and well controlled status-quo. They tend to lend their abilities to making sure the Ivory Tower lives up to those values. They keep a keen eye on events and individuals, making sure nobody rocks the boat. <i>Or else.</i><br /> <br /> Many of these vampires keep a staff of carefully conditioned spies and bodyguards to protect themselves.<br /> <br /> Childer are typically picked from those who serve the needs of the sire, clan and sect. People who show themselves capable in maintaining the environment the clan needs. Often they come from the sire's ghoul retinue, going through a period of assessment and grooming - followed by yet another one after the embrace.<br /> <br /> A lot of them develop intense paranoia and control problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>These are cool, I think the, and can see the, being players in the Camarilla. I wonder if Auspex would be an appropriate Discipline for them? I could imagine vampires of this type who are terribly crippled or very cautious remaining in their haven while sending their minds out into the world to command pawns or spy on enemies.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482055-alternative-v-tm-creating-new-clans?p=1482086#post1482086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:36px\">Yara-Ma</span><br /> The Yara-Ma of Australian wilds are little known, and less cared for. Kindred view them as a dangerous threat for their ability to walk around in the sun without fear. Despite this, members of the bloodline rarely take part in vampiric politics, and often prefer to sleep in fig trees most days, where they wait for mortals to rest under before they attack. Their ability to walk in the sun makes many believe that they are not in fact kindred at all.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Nickname:</b> Drop Bears</span><br /> <br /> <b>Sect:</b><span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> The Drop Bears rarely participate in modern politics and will rarely join the Sabbat or Camarilla. However, both sects will often hire the Yara-Ma as day-time assassins.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Appearance:</b><span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> Yara-Ma often twist their features and traits to look more koala like to become less noticeable in the trees. However, just as many in the clan will take their time to look especially monstrous if given the chance.<br /> <br /> <b>Haven:</b> The Drops Bears often hunt in the wilds and will most often make their home within trees and caves. The bloodline often prefers to sleep in fig trees, a practice taught from sire to childer.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Background:</b> Yara-Ma only embrace individuals who show a resilience and ability to survive harsh environments. People who resist their feeding are often embraced after a long observational period.<br /> <br /> <b>Clan Disciplines: </b>Fortitude, Potence, Vicissitude<br /> <br /> <b>Weakness: </b>The Yara-Ma have nothing to fear from the sun, and do not need to sleep during the day. However, they instead feel the urge to sleep at night and often will not wake without great difficulty. The Drop Bear\u2019s Humanity/Path rating is considered 2 dots lower for waking and remaining active at night. This weakness is the primary reason the drop bears do not take part in the undead's politics.<br /> <br /> <b>Organization:</b> Drop Bears are solitary by nature and will only mentor their childer for a month at most.</div> </div> </div> </div>These are cool as well, though like the savages, these might have to be relegated to the status of bloodline. I can\u2019t see these day walking Australian koala vampires being a major player in the world of vampires.<br /> <br /> So let me give a rundown of our setting:<br /> <br /> <b>Camarilla:</b><br /> Cicatrix<br /> Netjeru<br /> Dracul<br /> <br /> <b>Sabbat</b>:<br /> Pontiki<br /> <br /> <b>Independant</b>:<br /> Cecaelia<br /> Hags (independent until I hear otherwise)<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodlines</b>:<br /> Mara-Ma<br /> Savages<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll introduce another one soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1129,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","user":"Sergeant Brother","date":". 05-28-2022, 10:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-27T23:46:17-07:00","id":1482131,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\">Netjeru</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">The Netjeru have their origins in ancient Egypt among the ruling noble families and high priests of the Old Kingdom. For thousands of years the Netjeru have preserved their religious traditions, worshipping the gods of ancient Egypt and practices their necromantic magics. More strangely, they have also preserved ancient bloodlines as well - the blood of ancient Egyptian kinds still flows within the veins of inbred ghoul families who serve the Netjeru and who the Netjeru almost exclusively embrace from. The Netjeru are extremely conservative and hierarchal, with harsh punishments for disobedience or heresy. They also believe that their bloodlines are superior and that other mortals should serve them. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Nickname</b>: Mummies</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Sect</b>: The Netjeru are staunch members of the Camarilla. They belief that the elders should rule and that childer should obey. Those Netjeru who join the Sabbat are hunted ruthlessly by the parent Clan. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Appearance</b>: As part of their ritual embrace, the Netjeru go through a process much like mummification. This leaves their bodies as withered corpses covered in linen wrapping. Most wear ornate garments of ancient design over their bandages, many with golden masks crafted to resemble their living faces. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Haven</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">The Netjeru see themselves as royalty and seek the most opulent dwellings from which to rule their subjects. This often includes grand mansions or even ancient buildings, particularly in their homeland of Egypt. The Netjeru surround themselves with revenant family members as well as conventional mortal ghouls, to serve them and act as their herd, they seldom interact with normal humans.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Background</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Almost all Netjeru are embraced from one of the families who claim ancestry from ancient Egyptian kings. These families have inbred with each other for millennia and often have odd characteristics as a result. They tend to be somewhat alienated from mainstream society, even having exotic accents as their first language tends to be ancient Egyptian.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Clan Disciplines</b>: Dominate, Fortitude, Necromancy</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Weakness</b>: The Netjeru cannot embrace normally, their embrace requires a long process where the childe is slain and their body carefully preserved, with organs removed, and flesh wrapped is specially prepared bandages - mummification. The end result leaves the childe with an appearance of zero, like a Nosferatu, though the bandages reduce the shock of seeing one somewhat. Those Netjeru who are not embraced in this way do not gain the full advantages of vampirism and are treated as thin blooded vampires (15th generation) and have that flaw instead. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Organization</b>: The Netjeru are highly organized and have are ruled by a High Priest, usually eldest conscious Netjeru, who has beneath him advisers from each of the royal families who serve the Netjeru. Beneath them is a hierarchy based on region and family affiliation. Despite the strict hierarchy, sometimes the families feud amongst each other and this can undermine Clan loyalty - though they always try to maintain a facade of complete cooperation. </span><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-28T05:59:56-07:00","id":1482144,"title":"","content":"We\u2019ve got to have at least one classic\u2026<br /> <br /> <b>Dracul</b><br /> <br /> When Vlad Tepes offered hospitality to a nameless wanderer and shared with him his struggles in protecting Wallachia from the Ottomans, the stranger offered Vlad the power to defend his people for eternity if he would but make himself an enemy of his enemy; the Biblical God.<br /> <br /> He accepted and at Scholomance, an underground fortress in the Carpithian mountains, he studied the blackest of arts under the stranger for seven years until one day the stranger vanished\u2026 never to be seen again.<br /> <br /> Vlad, now commanding the powers of Hell in the name of his sire, whom he knew only as The Dragon, returned to his realm in Wallachia and began to form his own brood.<br /> <br /> The other clans, whose founders are millennia upon millennia older, at first regarded these upstarts as a joke, for it so clashed with established dogma that the Second Generation had long been destroyed, but between the story of his creation, the powers he displayed and even the Methuselahs of other clans being unable to bend his will it was concluded that somehow this relative neonate was the childe of either a forgotten member of the Second Generation or perhaps even Caine himself.<br /> <br /> To set the others at ease, Vlad Dracula willingly joined his Clan to the fledgling Camarilla and they remain among the most devoted to the success of that institution. He also suggested the creation of cover stories to discredit stories of vampires by making their fictional representations a part of popular culture; using whispers to one Bram Stoker as a test case with similar methods to inspire authors such as Rice, Whedon, Rein-Hagen and Meyers to make vampires into something everyone believes are fictional and so anyone who claims to have seen one is automatically discredited.<br /> <br /> <b>Clan Disciplines:</b> Blood Sorcery, Daimonion, Protean. While they are not \u201cin Clan\u201d disciplines, animalism and dominate and the physical disciplines are known by enough elders that one of the Dracul rarely has to step outside of the Clan to obtain them.<br /> <br /> <b>Clan Weakness:</b> Your soul is corrupt and seeks to corrupt others. You make virtue checks at +1 difficulty and, when you feed from someone you consider \u201cpure\u201d you must make a Self-Control check (difficulty 8) to resist giving them some of your blood (making them a ghoul or vampire depending on whether you drained them dry or not).<br /> <br /> <b>Organization:</b> Most members of the Dracul were innocents who were blood bound and as ghouls made to perform sinful and debasing acts before finally being embraced. The most promising candidates are sent to Scholomance, from which Vlad Dracula now rules his Clan and instructs his brood in the secrets of blood magic and the command of even darker powers.<br /> <br /> Accidental childer (typically those killed during a frenzy where the sire doesn\u2019t even remember following the compulsion to share their blood) are essentially the Clan\u2019s antitribu (typically joining the Anarchs or Sabbat) and in place of the compulsion to inflict their blood upon the innocent, instead crave the blood of other vampires (with a self-control check needed to avoid drinking a vampire they feed from dry).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T06:39:21-07:00","id":1482247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482055-alternative-v-tm-creating-new-clans?p=1482100#post1482100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.<br /> <br /> These are cool, I think the, and can see the, being players in the Camarilla. I wonder if Auspex would be an appropriate Discipline for them? I could imagine vampires of this type who are terribly crippled or very cautious remaining in their haven while sending their minds out into the world to command pawns or spy on enemies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Auspex should probably swap with Obfuscate. I probably would've picked it in the first place if I hadn't forgotten about it.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> Had another idea inspired by ants, of all things. Honestly not sure how playable this is, so it might be bloodline material.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Polyergus</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Curse:</b> Mere mortal blood is like water to this clan, only the vitae of other vampires can sate their hunger. Taking blood as payment for services is the most socially acceptable way to feed. However, due to the obvious issues inherent in drinking from vampires, historically some Polyergus have been known to drain their victims dry or, better, keep a rotational larder of thralls or staked victims. As their own clan is rather difficult to sustain, kidnapping the childer of other clans who feed on mortal blood - or more likely, getting a vampire to sire a blood doll as a boon - is a common way to get food in that manner. Those who keep herds are very &quot;fond&quot; of them, in their own horrible, blood bond addled way.<br /> <br /> Other clans have found that promising to donate an upstart to the cannibals is a rather effective threat. <br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> Auspex, Vicissitude, Presence<br /> Thieves of thoughts, souls and faces who walk amongst society undetected. A Polyergus learns her target through listening and watching his every move and emotion, until the time is right and she catches him off guard, mesmerises him, eats him if he's a vampire, and steals his face and life. Presence is also used in tandem with the kiss and blood bonds as a form of conditioning upon a herd to keep them subservient. Other uses include toning down the hostility they're commonly met with.<br /> The clan has a tradition of blood sorcery, and have invented several rituals that make their hunts easier, but pay out of clan costs to learn it. Other popular choices include the physical disciplines and Dominate. Even with the Kiss and the ability to detach limbs like clay, vampires tend to be harder to feed on than mortals.<br /> <br /> <b>Sect:</b> Sabbat. <br /> For all that nobody likes them, their weakness makes them vulnerable to blood bonds, their flesh crafting is invaluable for blending in with kine, and their shape shifting capabilities makes them excellent at espionage and assassinations. Historically they've made very useful thralls, and their own elders certainly weren't above enslaving their childer.<br /> The Polyergus were large proponents of the Anarch revolt specifically due to that particular issue, so had no reason to join when the Camarilla wanted to put that status quo back in place (letting cannibals run loose is a strangely unpopular idea).<br /> The vinculum also somewhat does away with the side effect of that pesky feeding problem.<br /> <br /> There is a small number of the clan amongst the Camarilla, where they are a closely watched and invaluable tool in maintaining the Masquerade. Their devotion to the sect is ironclad - it's not like they could feel otherwise, after all.<br /> Another number, who value their humanity as much as their freedom and are disgusted by the Sabbat, are independent. Many use their ability to change identity and &quot;age&quot; to live amongst mortals, preying on vampires who abuse their neighbours while doing their best to stay under the local Prince's radar. Others do a quiet business trading their services for secrecy and protection.<br /> <br /> Prospective childer are usually the types who can spin a good lie, don't mind getting their hands filthy and can go unnoticed. Charm is also valued. These vampires were often, though not always, career criminals. Traffickers, spies, identity thieves, hitmen, vagrants, con artists and actors come to mind.<br /> Fledglings and neonates are often dependent on their sires, who pay them vitae from their own herds in payment for obedience and competent service. <br /> <br /> As vicissitude also allows the user to take on monstrous form, there's a popular opinion that, between that and their diet, these guys aren't really the same creatures as other vampires but some other kind of monster that hunts them. Some Polyergus agree, claiming to be purer than those who feed on weaker blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 05-29-2022, 09:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T14:19:54-07:00","id":1482289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482055-alternative-v-tm-creating-new-clans?p=1482247#post1482247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, Auspex should probably swap with Obfuscate. I probably would've picked it in the first place if I hadn't forgotten about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool. You could potentially swap Fortitude with Auspex to emphasize their fragility, depending on if you prefer Auspex, Dominate, and Obfuscate or Auspex, Dominate, and Fortitude. <br /> <br /> I may change some of the Disciplines of some of my Clans I made.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Had another idea inspired by ants, of all things. Honestly not sure how playable this is, so it might be bloodline material.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Polyergus</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Curse:</b> Mere mortal blood is like water to this clan, only the vitae of other vampires can sate their hunger. Taking blood as payment for services is the most socially acceptable way to feed. However, due to the obvious issues inherent in drinking from vampires, historically some Polyergus have been known to drain their victims dry or, better, keep a rotational larder of thralls or staked victims. As their own clan is rather difficult to sustain, kidnapping the childer of other clans who feed on mortal blood - or more likely, getting a vampire to sire a blood doll as a boon - is a common way to get food in that manner. Those who keep herds are very &amp;quot;fond&amp;quot; of them, in their own horrible, blood bond addled way.<br /> <br /> Other clans have found that promising to donate an upstart to the cannibals is a rather effective threat. <br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> Auspex, Vicissitude, Presence<br /> Thieves of thoughts, souls and faces who walk amongst society undetected. A Polyergus learns her target through listening and watching his every move and emotion, until the time is right and she catches him off guard, mesmerises him, eats him if he's a vampire, and steals his face and life. Presence is also used in tandem with the kiss and blood bonds as a form of conditioning upon a herd to keep them subservient. Other uses include toning down the hostility they're commonly met with.<br /> The clan has a tradition of blood sorcery, and have invented several rituals that make their hunts easier, but pay out of clan costs to learn it. Other popular choices include the physical disciplines and Dominate. Even with the Kiss and the ability to detach limbs like clay, vampires tend to be harder to feed on than mortals.<br /> <br /> <b>Sect:</b> Sabbat. <br /> For all that nobody likes them, their weakness makes them vulnerable to blood bonds, their flesh crafting is invaluable for blending in with kine, and their shape shifting capabilities makes them excellent at espionage and assassinations. Historically they've made very useful thralls, and their own elders certainly weren't above enslaving their childer.<br /> The Polyergus were large proponents of the Anarch revolt specifically due to that particular issue, so had no reason to join when the Camarilla wanted to put that status quo back in place (letting cannibals run loose is a strangely unpopular idea).<br /> The vinculum also somewhat does away with the side effect of that pesky feeding problem.<br /> <br /> There is a small number of the clan amongst the Camarilla, where they are a closely watched and invaluable tool in maintaining the Masquerade. Their devotion to the sect is ironclad - it's not like they could feel otherwise, after all.<br /> Another number, who value their humanity as much as their freedom and are disgusted by the Sabbat, are independent. Many use their ability to change identity and &amp;quot;age&amp;quot; to live amongst mortals, preying on vampires who abuse their neighbours while doing their best to stay under the local Prince's radar. Others do a quiet business trading their services for secrecy and protection.<br /> <br /> Prospective childer are usually the types who can spin a good lie, don't mind getting their hands filthy and can go unnoticed. Charm is also valued. These vampires were often, though not always, career criminals. Traffickers, spies, identity thieves, hitmen, vagrants, con artists and actors come to mind.<br /> Fledglings and neonates are often dependent on their sires, who pay them vitae from their own herds in payment for obedience and competent service. <br /> <br /> As vicissitude also allows the user to take on monstrous form, there's a popular opinion that, between that and their diet, these guys aren't really the same creatures as other vampires but some other kind of monster that hunts them. Some Polyergus agree, claiming to be purer than those who feed on weaker blood. </div> </div> </div>Those are cool. I think that they would have trouble as Camarilla or Independent, but as the Sabbat they work, both with the Vaulderie and the social network. They make sense being allied to the Pontiki, who lack the social control ability of and could help them procure vampiric blood.<br /> <br /> Speaking on the Pontiki, I think I\u2019ll switch out their Auspex for Animalism, which I was seriously considering to start with and now switching to Animalism will reduce overlap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T21:16:12-07:00","id":1482340,"title":"","content":"Our alternative setting so far:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Camarilla:</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Cicatrix: Auspex, Dominate, Fortitude</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Netjeru: Dominate, Fortitude, Necromancy</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Dracul: Daimoinon, Protean, Sorcery</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Bagava: Animalism, Potence, Presence</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Sabbat</b>:</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Pontiki: Animalism, Celerity, Obfuscate</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Polyergus: Auspex, Presence, Vicissitude </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Independant</b>:</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Cecaelia: Fortitude, Presence, Protean</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Hags: Animalism, Obfuscate, Sorcery</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Bloodlines</b>:</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Mara-Ma: Fortitude, Potence, Vicissitude</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Savages: Fortitude, Potence, Protean</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\">Bagava</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">The Bagava were among the warlords of the ancient Indo-Aryans who conquered much of Europe and Southern Asia. They were a Clan of warriors who believed in crushing or at least conquering the weak. Over the course of millennia, this attitude has persisted if only taking on different forms. The Bagava believe that struggle is essential to life and unlike, that the strong must vanquish the weak for the betterment of nations, species, or even Clans. In ancient days they were warlords and chieftains of tribal peoples, in antiquity they gravities towards the Spartans and their harsh lifestyle. In the Middle Ages they were feudal knights. Later in the 19th and 20th centuries they fully embraced the eugenics movement and Social Darwinism. Over the millennia they have carefully bred a number of animal breeds for ideal service and even have a number of human lineages who have been eugenically bred for excellence and many Bagava are embraced from these lines. In the last several decades, the Clan has declined somewhat in political power both among kindred and kine.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Nickname</b>: Bullies</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Sect</b>: The Bagava are members of the Camarilla. They consider themselves the rightful rulers of mortal and vampire alike and so are drawn to the Camarilla and help organize it. There are some who join the Anarchs or Sabbat though, who believe that the Camarilla is too orderly to allow the strong to truly crush the weak. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Appearance</b>: the Bagava are usually attractive and fit, only those mortals who are flawless physical specimens are chosen for the embrace, only those who have gray physical prowess and usually combat ability. Bagava are seldom embraced in old age or young, so are usually young to middle aged adults. Most Bagava are men, though a few women are embraced into the Clan. They typically wear highly quality but also practical clothing.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Haven</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Bagava usually have opulent but we\u2019ll defendable havens. Large mansions surrounded by fences and security precautions. They usually prefer something outside of the heart of large cities, where their animal ghouls wont be as conspicuous. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Background</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Many Bagava are drawn from military or sports backgrounds, places where people are tested physically or even mentally. There are a number of family lines who the Bagava have been eugenically breeding for generations and many Bagava are drawn from these lineages. In the last few hundred years, some Bagava choose to embrace their childer for mental rather than physical excellence, choosing scientists and scholars, but even then they still must meet certain physical standards.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Clan Disciplines</b>: Animalism, Potence, Presence</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Weakness</b>: the bite of the Bagava causes no pleasure, only the sensation one might expect from being pierced by sharp teeth. It cannot paralyze foes nor entice them to receive the bliss of the kiss. Many Bagava believe that it is their destiny to struggle and fight for their blood, though some acquire it through more subtle means.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Organization</b>: The Bagava have a semi-feudal organization. Regions are controlled by a ruling Bagava lord and all Bagava within that region must pay homage and swear fealty to that elder, then beneath them are lords of small regions who receive similar oaths from lesser Bagava within. Sometimes there are wars between those lords or even revolts. There is no central ruler ship of the Clan.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T11:43:14-07:00","id":1482390,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:24px\">The Children of Veles</span><br /> Origin:</b><br /> The obscure vampiric Bloodline known as \u201cThe Children of Veles\u201d originated in the Slavic regions during the high medieval period. They are one of the oldest and now, almost forgotten weapons of the Carpathian Tzimisce during the large-scale conflicts and open war they waged against the nascent Clan Tremere.<br /> Most kindred historians will, undoubtedly, during their long studies over mouldy old tomes, find some notion about the creation of the Gargoyle Bloodline and how this, one of the greatest known kindred atrocities, would turn the war in the Tremeres favour during the battles along the Slavic border and into Tzimisce homeland. What is far less known is how the Tzimisce answered this escalating conflict and at what lengths they were willing to go, to achieve victory.<br /> <br /> Truth to be told, the Tzimisce in the Slavic region were not sitting idly while they had their territory constantly assaulted by Clan Tremere. In a unified effort they pushed their spiritual sorcery to, new, previously unseen heights, in order to stave of the waves of Gargoyles that kept attacking their settlements, keeps and castles.<br /> With a large portion of the Clan working with the increased focus on the arcane and occult, not only did the effort bring about new Koldunic Sorcery Rituals and Kraina, but also resulted in the creation of the first, artificial hybrid lineage of Kindred, in the form of a small Bloodline: The Children of Veles. They were so aptly named because of the similarities between the new vampiric lineage and the mythological Slavic God of The Underworld, Trickery and Shapeshifting, Veles.<br /> <br /> The leaders and instigators behind the effort never told their Clan mates about their various projects and kept those a well-guarded secret until the many labours had born fruit. What little is known is that at some point in time, one of the pioneers, an ancient and powerful Koldun, decided to meet the Gargoyles in open combat with a new breed of kindred, artificially created and subservient to their Tzimisce masters. This was ironically inspired by the Tremers creation of the Gargoyle Bloodline, which the Fiends so despised. In order to meet the Gargoyles and their Tremere masters in open combat, a new mockery of life, or rather unlife, had to be created. The vision was simple but effective, they needed a more combat capable and durable, artificial Bloodline of kindreds that was expandable, easy to produce and specialized at hunting and killing kindred and human victims of the Tzimisce Clan.<br /> The process of how these first \u201cChildren\u201d were created have been all but lost to time, only possessed by the highest ranking Kolduns of Clan Tzimisce and used only sparsely in times of need. The process involved binding a powerful spirit to a chosen human\u2019s body, with the aid of powerful ritualistic binding tattoos, and then subsequently draining the body of all its blood until clinical death occurred, after which the dead body was forcefully feed a combination of altered Tzimisce and Nosferatu Vitae, the exact procedure unknown to all outside the creator Kolduns.<br /> <br /> If successful, the ritual would allow the deceased individual to be raised as a newly embraced kindred of the Children of Veles, having access to all previous memories and skills they had in life. However, the body would only provide a physical form and access to its former mind. The soul of the original human individual would be gone, having passed on into the afterlife as it was replaced by a powerful, but still subservient, spirit of the Carpathian soil, who, as the body and mind fused with the spirits essence, gave rise to a newly formed entity in the form of a kindred of the Children\u2019s Bloodline.<br /> <br /> This new individual would be fiercely loyal to Clan Tzimisce, have an unusual aptitude for the spiritual and otherworldly, as well as being of the newly created Bloodline. These fledglings would then be given over to senior kindred mentors that would train and educate them into their new roles as assassins, hunters and warriors.<br /> Contrary to the original Gargoyles, The Children of Veles were in all aspects \u201ctrue kindred\u201d and could embrace new members into the fold if they saw the time and opportunity to do so.<br /> <br /> <b>Organization:</b><br /> Almost non-existent. On their own the Children organizes into small covens of loosely affiliated groups or cells. There is no singular leader, rather the entirety of the leaders from all groups/cells has a vote and gets to speak for that group. Rarely, another leader structure is used, but even then, there is never any \u201cOne-man rules all\u201d mentality. The short answer to why is simple: It\u2019s too vulnerable having a single individual sitting on all the power of the collective coven. Better to have a number of leaders if someone meets final death and then appoint a new leader from the worthy, then losing all structure and hierarchy when one falls.<br /> <br /> Outside of their own, they are almost always accompanying a Tzimisce, either as bodyguards in disguise or as tracker/hunter pairs in service to the Clan of Fiends. The Tzimisce have the highest authority, at least that\u2019s what everyone agrees to. The truth is more complicated: The highest-ranking War heroes of the Children carries the same or even higher standing among their own than even the most esteemed Koldun could hope to attain. The only exception to this rule would be if one of the ancient Tzimisce who created the Bloodline in ages past where to emerge and ask for service.<br /> <br /> <b>Culture:</b><br /> The Children are spiritual and ritualistic while also being pragmatic and opportunistic. They all try to become the ultimate hunter, but the views on this subject are as varied as the individuals who constitutes the coven in its entirety. They tend to embrace seldom and only when a dire need demands such actions.<br /> <br /> <b>General Information:</b><br /> <br /> <b>Name:</b> The Children of Veles<br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames:</b> Derogatory; Bogeymen or Cannibals, Polite; Hunters or Beasts.<br /> <br /> <b>Antediluvian:</b> None, as an Artificial Bloodline, or Tzimisce and Nosferatu<br /> <br /> <b>Faction:</b> Independent, Nominally Sabbat Affiliated<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> Obfuscate, Carnophagia and Potence<br /> <br /> <b>Weakness:</b> The Children are sensitive to spells and effects that can target spirits of the land. To resist such spells/effects the Child rolls Willpower \u2013 2 (Difficulty depending on the level and number of successes on the activation roll of an offensive power). The Child will also be susceptible to alterations in his or her path rating, which in turn twists and mutates the body in new and alien ways. The lower the path rating the more monstrous the kindred becomes, while a high rating maintains a humane appearance.<br /> <br /> <b>Clan Symbol:</b> The Tzimisce Dragon Ouroboros at the center of a ritualistic circle with arcane marks and symbols corresponding to the planets, moon and sun.<br /> <br /> <b>Modern Night Child of Veles:</b> If there are any Children still alive tonight, they are well hidden and mostly keep to themselves.<br /> <br /> <b>New Bloodline Discipline: Carnophagia</b><br /> <br /> <b>Basic Discipline Levels: </b><br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Devouring Maw </b>- Allows the user to draw Vitae from the victim while making a standard bite attack.<br /> <br /> <b><b>System: </b></b>This power is always active once learned and allows the vampire to both perform a bite attack and feed as one single action.<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022 <b>Blood Memories </b>- Allows the user to gain memories and skim surface thoughts from a target by drinking their blood.<br /> <br /> <b><b>System: </b></b>Not complete yet!<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 <b>Bloody Perseverance </b>- By imbuing a dismembered limb/remain of a kill with Vitae, the decaying process is halted and the blood stored in this way preserved indefinitely until withdrawn by a vampire with this power at a later date.<br /> <br /> <b><b>System: </b></b>Not complete yet!<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 <b>Sheep\u2019s Clothing </b>- By flaying a fresh victim, the skin can be transformed into a leathery, full-body armour that, while worn, also disguises the vampire as the dead individual in question. This power can also be used on animals with the same requirements and effects.<br /> <br /> <b><b>System: </b></b>Not complete yet!<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 <b>Hunting Ground </b>- The vampire marks his chosen territory by spilling vitae around its borders and when activated, the vampire knows whenever an individual enters the territory and gains bonuses to any hunt and combat rolls within his chosen hunting ground. He is also capable of knowing wherever a person entering his domain is supernatural or not in nature.<br /> <br /> <b><b>System: </b></b>Not complete yet!<br /> <br /> <b>Advanced Discipline Levels: </b><br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 <b>Infected Wounds </b>- All damage inflicted by this power can be \u201cstored\u201d and activated later, when it triggers, old wounds reopen and inflict the old, suffered, damage once more.<br /> <br /> <b><b>System: </b></b>Not complete yet!<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 <b>Moroi </b>- Transforms the vampire into a huge chameleon-like predatory beast that gains increased physical attributes (+3 in all the physical attributes), natural weapons with aggravated damage and a camouflaged skin which hides the vampire in all kinds of environments.<br /> <br /> <b><b>System: </b></b>Not complete yet!<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 <b>Predatory Adaptation </b>- The vampire\u2019s body will reflexively change to any stimuli in order to improve its survivability and chosen specialization while hunting.<br /> <br /> <b>System: </b>Not complete yet!<br /> <br /> <b>Combination Disciplines:</b><br /> <br /> <b>Gruesome Wards:</b> Carnophagia 3 + Animalism 3 (<b>Cost:</b> 24 Exp)<br /> This combination discipline lets the user place horrific trophies as a warning and markers for claimed territory. The user can then instantly know when someone is inside his chosen domain and gets a minor bonus to rolls made to hunt and kill the intruder.<br /> <br /> <b>System:</b> Not complete yet!<br /> <br /> <b>Appalling Lure:</b> Carnophagia 3 + Presence 4 (<b>Cost:</b> 28 Exp)<br /> By imbuing the remains of his victims with the alluring powers of Presence and placing the bones in mystical patterns around his territory, the user can attract and confuse potential victims, which will wander into the territory unknowingly and become lost or trapped.<br /> <br /> <b>System:</b> Not complete yet!<br /> <br /> <b>The Warding Flesh:</b> Carnophagia 4 + Vicissitude 3 (<b>Cost:</b> 30 Exp)<br /> This power imbues the flayed skin of a victim so that when worn by the user it inspires fear or even terror in onlookers unless they have a strong enough will to resist its effects. The skin also grants an armour rating of 3 when worn by the specific vampire which created it with this combination discipline.<br /> <br /> <b>System:</b> Not complete yet!<br /> <br /> <b>Trackers Mark:</b> Carnophagia 3 + Auspex 2 (<b>Cost:</b> 20 Exp)<br /> This power allows for the invisible marking of an individual whom the user can then faintly sense regarding relative distance and direction. It\u2019s usually used to mark unusual or powerful prey so that it can be found and killed when it\u2019s in a weak position and unable to properly defend itself.<br /> <br /> <b>System:</b> Not complete yet!<br /> <br /> <b>Ant-lion's Pit:</b> Carnophagia 3 + Protean 3 (<b>Cost:</b> 22 Exp)<br /> The vampire merges with the ground and ones a victim walks over his position, he makes the ground collapse and slide towards him in the center of the newly<br /> created pit of soil and sand. Victims trapped in this way can\u2019t escape unless they are extremely strong and durable or have friends nearby.<br /> <br /> <b>System: </b>Not complete yet!<br /> <br /> <b>The Flaying:</b> Carnophagia 4 + Animalism 3 + Vicissitude 3 (<b>Cost:</b> 32 Exp)<br /> This truly horrible power allows the user to slowly flay a human victim without killing them in the process, which ends in the ghouling of said victim. Thanks to the application of this combination discipline, the victim is forever-more skinless and grisly deformed, forced to live a continuing nightmare in which all they have left is their own, pitiful life and a maddening addiction to the domitor's blood. However, the transformation into a ghoul, by this combination discipline, does grant some unique benefits: Lethal claws, teeth and bone spurs as well as a natural armour 3 and another free dot of the Potence Discipline. The skin itself is in pristine condition and can be used for all other powers that require a human skin to be performed, such as the fourth power of the Carnophagia Discipline or The Warding Flesh Combination Discipline.<br /> <br /> <b>System:</b> Not complete yet!<br /> <br /> <b>Primordial Horror:</b> Carnophagia 5 + Presence 5 + Vicissitude 4 (<b>Cost:</b> 40 Exp)<br /> With this horrible combination discipline, the user physically and spiritually transforms into the very embodiment of mankind\u2019s oldest fears, gaining a monstrous form, befitting of a supernatural predator which hunts and devours humans and vampires alike. This form induces sheer terror into all but the strongest of minds, and is equipped with aggravated claws and teeth, natural armour of 3 and a + 3 dots increase in all physical attributes. Finally, all spilt blood in the vicinity of the user, using The Purest of Fears Combination Discipline, will start to crawl or trickle towards the vampire, as if he was the center of a gravitational well. All blood thus absorbed by the vampire in his monstrous form will automatically replenish his blood pool.<br /> <br /> <b>System: </b>Not complete yet!<br /> <br /> <b>Predatory Pets:</b> Carnophagia 3 + Presence 2 + Animalism 3 (<b>Cost:</b> 24 Exp)<br /> With this power the user are capable of ghouling and breeding naturally occurring vermin or predatory animals into gigantic, feral versions of their usual forms. These beasts are fiercely loyal and have a telepathic link with their domitor vampire. They also have lethal inflicting natural weapons and the normal bonuses of being ghouls in addition to the benefits of this power. The increased size confers a + 4 Physical Attributes, distributed as the Storyteller sees fit, and a natural lethal soak. The beasts created with this power can\u2019t survive without their regular upkeep of the domitor's Vitae and will start to starve to death without Vitae in their system at the point where a ghoul stops being a ghoul and reverts back to a mortal creature.<br /> <br /> <b>System: </b>Not complete yet!<br /> <br /> What do you guys think about the Children of Veles? Do they fit best as a Bloodline or a Clan? All feedback is appreciated and most welcome! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/533-daniel-p","name":"Daniel P","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T16:49:50-07:00","id":1482421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daniel P</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482055-alternative-v-tm-creating-new-clans?p=1482390#post1482390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you guys think about the Children of Veles? Do they fit best as a Bloodline or a Clan? All feedback is appreciated and most welcome! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>They\u2019re cool. I like them quite a bit. Your origin involves the Tzimisce and Tremere, which don\u2019t exist in this collaborative setting, so for them to fit in they would have to be tweaked slightly. They could be a Sabbat bloodline created by the Polyergus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T04:19:43-07:00","id":1482474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482055-alternative-v-tm-creating-new-clans?p=1482421#post1482421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They\u2019re cool. I like them quite a bit. Your origin involves the Tzimisce and Tremere, which don\u2019t exist in this collaborative setting, so for them to fit in they would have to be tweaked slightly. They could be a Sabbat bloodline created by the Polyergus.</div> </div> </div> </div>I loosely based the Polyergus on slave-making ants, and I didn't have the spiritual themes of the Tzimisce in mind while making them. Of course I never fleshed out their blood magic paradigm, so while I didn't have it in mind, dealing with spirits could be part of it. <br /> <br /> If you wanted to go that way: Their discipline kinda fits, the monstrous boogeyman angle fits, making a specialist servant caste fits. <br /> <br /> The next issue is that we don't have gargoyles or the omen war thus far, so there needs to be a reason for the Eastern European members of the Clan to decide they need to create them. As defences against attempts to exterminate them? Their subterfuge lends itself to fleeing and hiding, but if you lean into the larder-building and ant theme thing you could go for established &quot;nests&quot; of Polyergus that need defending.<br /> It might also work better if, like gargoyles, they're made from kidnapped fledglings from other clans fused with Polyergus blood and spirits.<br /> <br /> Otherwise they'll need to fit into either one of the established clans, or one that hasn't been created yet. Or make them self-created, somehow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 05-31-2022, 07:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-02T19:03:01-07:00","id":1482882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482055-alternative-v-tm-creating-new-clans?p=1482474#post1482474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I loosely based the Polyergus on slave-making ants, and I didn't have the spiritual themes of the Tzimisce in mind while making them. Of course I never fleshed out their blood magic paradigm, so while I didn't have it in mind, dealing with spirits could be part of it.<br /> <br /> If you wanted to go that way: Their discipline kinda fits, the monstrous boogeyman angle fits, making a specialist servant caste fits.<br /> <br /> The next issue is that we don't have gargoyles or the omen war thus far, so there needs to be a reason for the Eastern European members of the Clan to decide they need to create them. As defences against attempts to exterminate them? Their subterfuge lends itself to fleeing and hiding, but if you lean into the larder-building and ant theme thing you could go for established &quot;nests&quot; of Polyergus that need defending.<br /> It might also work better if, like gargoyles, they're made from kidnapped fledglings from other clans fused with Polyergus blood and spirits.<br /> <br /> Otherwise they'll need to fit into either one of the established clans, or one that hasn't been created yet. Or make them self-created, somehow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, a number of things would have to be changed to make it work out, considering that fact that we don\u2019t have any of the same sorts of dynamics or history, at least not yet. Maybe you and Daniel P can discuss it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\">Sukkal </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">The Sukkal have a long history as a Clan of scholars, philosophers, and theologians. In ancient days they documented the legends of the kindred and recorded histories of kindred and kind alike. They sought out mortals of great intellect or learning for the embrace and have often influenced vampiric politics with their deep thoughts. Often kindreds of great power used the Sukkal as advisers and allies.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">In the Middle Ages, Sukkal philosophers popularized the ideas of rights and liberties, ideas which helped to foment the Anarch Revolts. Many of the Sukkal joined with the Anarch Revolt, though the mainstream of the Clan stood by the elders and as advisers among the Clans, they helped the elders to create the system that would later become the Camarilla. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">At some point during the Renaissance the Clan began to undergo a change. Formerly aloof scholars and advisers, the Sukkal began to adopt an ideology of humanism - that vampires should be compassionate towards mortals,should not use their powers to control humans but rather to protect them. Some say that this was an ideological change by the Clan founder himself, becoming more humane and making it difficult for his descendants to drink the blood of mortals. The Sukkal began to use their influence with the Camarilla to push the institution in a kinder and gentler direction: sparing human life, avoiding manipulating humans, seeking to maintain their humanity. Because many vampires in power are resistant to this, the Sukkal often find themselves in the position of Anarchs yet again and they often are at odds with the Camarilla leadership. Some still serve as advisers to princes or justicars. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Nickname</b>: Vegetarians</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Sect</b>: the Sukkal are officially members of the Camarilla and many high ranking members of other Clans often keep a Sukkal scholar or adviser on hand. Outside of this, the Sukkal are very prominent among Anarchs. There are also a sizable contingent of Sukkal antitribu among the Sabbat.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Appearance</b>: The Sukkal vary in appearance, as few are selected for the embrace based on physical prowess or beauty, but rather for knowledge, intellect, or ideology. Often older people are selected for the embrace, but this isn\u2019t universal. Vampires of this Clan often dress in formal, yet understated, fashions. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Haven</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">The Sukkal like to have havens near places of learning or cultural importance. Universities are favorite locations for Sukkal havens. Sometimes they select havens outside of the inner cities and depend on their power over animals to supply them with sustenance.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Background</b>:Historically, the Sukkal came from academic backgrounds, even priests, philosophers, or intellectuals. Those sorts of people still comprise many of those embraced into the Clan, but more recently they tend to prefer people with a record of humanitarian activity - activists, health care professionals, social or charity workers, etc. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Clan Disciplines</b>: Animalism, Auspex, Celerity</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Weakness</b>:</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">The Sukkal the blood of humans tastes bitter to the Sukkal and they must drink two points of blood from a human to gain one blood point. They do not suffer from this effect when drinking the blood of vampires or animals. Furthermore, their base maximum Blood Pool is their Humanity, not 10. So a 10th generation Sukkal with a Humanity of 8 could only hold up to 11 Blood Points.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Organization</b>: the Clan has no formal organization, though the Sukkal do tend to keep firendly relationships with each other and share information or aid each other whenever possible. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><br /> </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Antitribu:</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Antitribu of the Sukkal will claim that the humanitarian change was the shifting will of the Antediluvians and that they, rejecting him as they do, were able to resist the change. What ever the reason, Antitribu of the Sukkal are different than the Camarilla version of the Clan. In a Dark Ages setting, this is the dominant version of the Clan. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Disciplines: Auspex, Celerity, Dominate</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Weakness: the Antitribu of this Clan suffer from their traditional weakness that extends through the ages. When the Sukkal encounters an interesting new idea, be it science, philosophy, or social issues, it must succeed at a Self Control or Instincts roll with a difficulty of 6 or become either lost in thought or embroiled in conversation over the topic. This effect lasts for a scene but may be ended prematurely by spending a point of Willpower. </span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-03T23:38:25-07:00","id":1483022,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:22px\">Vegulans</span><br /> The ancient myth of the clan claims its founder was once a powerful mage, whom the first vampire embraced as an experiment. The result was Vegas, the founder of all blood sorcery. Devastation at the loss of his magic, Vegas began experimenting with the blood. From these experiments, he discovered the Path of Blood, and by extension all other sorceries of the blood.<br /> <br /> <b>Nickname: </b>The Fallen Stars<br /> <br /> <b>Sect: </b>The Vegalin are predominately Camarilla aligned. As a clan, they desire unity and structure and knowledge of all things. However, since any mage that is embraced will become a Fallen Star means many Vegulans can easily find themselves in any political sect.<br /> <br /> <b>Background: </b>The Fallen come from one of two backgrounds. One is those sired by another Vegulan, which makes up the bulk of the clan. However, a rare few were once members of the Awakened, and the power of the blood made them into a Fallen Star. Vegulan Elders often seek out of clan embraces in order to add them to the fold, something many such Vegulans do not wish at all.<br /> <br /> <b>Clan Disciplines: </b>The Fallen Stars have the innate ability to learn all disciplines equally and spontaneously. The cost to increase any discipline is the same as the Caitiff.<br /> <br /> <b>Weakness: </b>Magic runs in the veins of all the Fallen Stars. All Vegulans suffer from some Supernatural flaw at character creation, which does not give you additional freebie points and does not count against your maximum flaws. In addition, the Fallen Stars all suffer a +2 Difficulty to hide their Supernatural nature to all would be observers.<br /> <br /> <b>Organization: </b>The Vegulan clan seeks to unite under a single banner and creed. At least, that is what many of the Elders seek, a desire which sees the clan collecting itself into a complicated web of blood bonds and political hierarchy. Status within the clan is determined purely by a member\u2019s knowledge of blood sorceries such as Thaumaturgy and Necromancy.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:22px\">The Strix</span><br /> Born from the original experiments of unknown blood sorcery, the Strix quickly spread to become the most common bloodline in the world. Acting more of an infection than an actual bloodline, Strix pose a deadly risk to the Masquerade where-ever they appear, as most of the bloodline become Wights before their first year. In addition, there are rumors that those who consume the blood of the Strix are doomed to become like them as well.<br /> <br /> <b>Nickname: </b>The Rabid<br /> <br /> <b>Sect: </b>The Sabbat at one time used the Strix as foot soldiers in their sieges and raids. However, the dangers of this practice became apparent, as many of the sect fell to the raging fangs of the Rabid. Since then, all cities and sects that discover even one Strix will quickly begin a Blood Hunt for the rest that are in the city.<br /> <br /> <b>Background: </b>Anyone can become a Rabid, as long as their luck is bad enough.<br /> <br /> <b>Clan Disciplines:</b> Potence, Celerity, and Foritude<br /> <br /> <b>Weakness: </b>The Rabid\u2019s curse is three-fold. First, all kine that fall to their fangs will rise again as if they were embraced, even if the corpse had never tasted vampiric vitae after death. Second, the Strix are all doomed to fall to the beast, and can never increase their Humanity, and can never adopt a Path of Enlightenment. Finally, their Intelligence and Conscience scores can never be higher than their Humanity rating.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:22px\">New Flaws</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Strix Rabies (5 Point Supernatural Flaw)</b></span><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You've tasted the blood of a Strix. You gain the Strix's weakness and replace your in-clan discipline list with that of the Strix. You do not lose levels in the Disciplines you knew, but further levels in those Disciplines are purchased at out-of-clan cost. You count as both a member of your original clan as well as a Strix, but anyone you embrace is always a Strix. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-04T14:25:46-07:00","id":1483074,"title":"","content":"Never really attempted to make a new clan wholesale in my games to be honest.<br /> <br /> That said, it's in no small part because i find throwing a &quot;lore reveal&quot; that casts one of the existing clans in a whole different perspective much simpler to implement, not to mention more impactful in the table than throwing a homebrew clan. Making the familiar once more unfamiliar to the experienced players and have them discuss and explore the implications.<br /> <br /> <br /> Some examples:<br /> - Giovanni are <b>not</b> descendants of the Cappadocians, never were, that's post-Anarch Revolt nonsense resulting of stupid collation of facts, rumors, half-truths and blatant lies. They and the <i><b>Lasombra </b></i>were branches of the same in-clan conspiracy, now each claiming to have consumed their antediluvian back in the middle ages during all the fighting in the italian peninsula, while glossing over the fact <b><i>its the same one</i></b>, ergo (at least) one of them is blatantly lying about who took down the founder of the &quot;nameless&quot; clan.<br /> <br /> - The Giovanni x Cappies &quot;purge&quot; was just a case of a rising clan backstabbing the flagging one for its many mortuary treasures - and truth be told, far more Cappadocians were destroyed <b><i>by witch-hunters, inquisitors and random christians with True Faith rising against the maniacal black death-inducing undead parasites ensonced within their own church</i></b> than by any venetian necromancers and their ilk.<br /> <br /> - Cappadocians in fact were the wayward branch of the brood of <b>Saulot</b>, those who refused the mystic teachings he brought along with the 3rd eye from the far east. Their clan status was a extensive work of fabrication, through their strong connection to early christian writers and involvment with establishing the Book of Nod and Caine Mythos as core tale of vampiric origins as presently known to most kindred.<br /> <br /> - Brujah's original brood is still around, quite active and well. They just call themselves <i><b>Toreador </b></i>and mostly nobody still knows or cares about an ancient consumed where the mists of mythology mix and lose themselves amidst the sands of time. The &quot;True Brujah&quot; of the Black Hand are utterly deluded fools.<br /> <br /> <br /> Oh yeah, i had forgotten that in some of my games <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shesha\" target=\"_blank\">Followers of Shesha</a> coming from India, Vietnam and other parts of southeast asia are very much a thing, along with their neverending conflict with the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bardo\" target=\"_blank\">Bardo</a> sects originating from the Tibetan Plateau and Hymalayan-bordered countries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 06-07-2022, 01:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-08T04:05:13-07:00","id":1483365,"title":"","content":"Speaking of half-forgotten canon hacks, in those games where i have <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shesha\" target=\"_blank\">Followers of Shesha</a> and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bardo\" target=\"_blank\">Bardo</a> among others filling the role of lords of night in a large chunk of Asia, i have as &quot;egyptian clan&quot; the Children of Sekhmet, a lineage of kindred that claim descent of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sekhmet#Roles\" target=\"_blank\">t</a>he <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sekhmet#Roles\" target=\"_blank\">bloodthirsty lion-goddess</a> instead of the setites. If she's a separate being or simply Ennoia and her childer under a different name/theming, well that's something to decide when a player decides to make a Gangrel or Sekhmeti in a game where both exist.... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> There's also a little something i conceived of late and have yet to find a game to fit them in, the Leshy.<br /> <br /> They started simply enough, with the idea of &quot;Gargoyles before the Gargoyles&quot;, kind of like the Nagaraja might be described as Tremere/Giovanni before the clan, so to speak.<br /> <br /> But then it dawned on me - Gangrel, Nosferatu, Tzimisce, all with qualities of shapechanging or grotesque through their powers and/or weaknesses, all with a propensity for distant, neglectful or downright abusive sires that will embrace and abandon their childer as either survival test, petty punishment/revenge, when not thrown them as disposable cannon fodder, not to mention Animalism.<br /> <br /> Does one even <b><i>require </i></b>awful blood magic experimentation for the lines between the rejected childer of those clans to blur, blend and shift into something else altogether?<br /> <br /> And so came to be the idea of &quot;<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leshy\" target=\"_blank\">they of the forest</a>&quot; a peculiar motley of beings that muddles the lines between bloodline, clans, Caitiff, coven and more in older nights and mostly subsumed, forgotten or consumed amidst the greater disorder of the Anarch Revolt, fall of clans, rise of others and the birth of modern kindred sects.<br /> <br /> Mostly. In some plains, groves, fields and sometimes even parks within urban areas, secluded from the eyes of most mortals or social kindred, strange calls, keens &amp; songs fueled by the power of blood are sung and the beasts will listen and gather to secretive nocturnal revelries of these self-made fauns and satyrs that frolick and feast, but not on.....wine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 06-08-2022, 05:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}